message: "If you use Priveria or build on this work, please cite the paper below."
title: "From Static DPIAs to Living Privacy Threat Registers for AI Governance"
authors:
  - family-names: Kompella
    given-names: Vivek
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher"
  - family-names: Jain
    given-names: Aashita
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher"
abstract: >-
  Data Protection Impact Assessments (DPIAs) are supposed to help organizations
  reason about high-risk processing before harm occurs, but in practice they
  often become one-time approval documents that no longer describe AI systems as
  data sources, model versions, vendors, prompts, tools, retention behavior, and
  autonomy levels change after release. This preprint develops the idea of a
  living DPIA: a structured privacy threat register that links processing
  context, legal reasoning, AI risk signals, mitigation ownership, and reusable
  evidence, using Priveria — an open-source prototype built by the authors — as a
  reference implementation.
keywords:
